      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Maillard reaction involves a complex sequence of reactions between amino acids and reducing sugars, leading to the formation of new compounds with distinct flavors, aromas, and colors. At the molecular level, reducing sugars like glucose react with amino acids to form initial products, such as imino compounds. The concentration of reducing sugars influences the rate of non-enzymatic browning. High concentrations of reducing sugars provide more reacting sites, allowing the reaction to progress faster. However, extremely high concentrations can lead to undesirable side products.",
